ts=2026-09-09T09:39:40.393Z type=context scope=ai-pulse content="ai-pulse Epic 2 (config-pack engine) done and open as stacked PR #20 (base epic/1-opencode-provider = PR #19). domains/ holds packs (ai, mac-apps); PULSE_DOMAIN env selects; sources are briefing(config, opts) with AI defaults; dashboard renders generically by category+variant via render-core.mjs + GET /api/domain. FR6 verified: default = byte-identical AI app. Epic日发布 3 (dendievel.me design pass) still deferred. Note: specs/ is gitignored (local-only) per repo convention." issue=#20 tags=epic2,config-pack,pr-open,stacked
ts=2026-09-09T11:06:04.950Z type=context scope=ai-pulse content="ai-pulse Epic 3 design: TWO user rejections shaped it. 1st: green-on-dark token swap (\"not looking like my website\"). 2nd: exact-colors light port still read as Jarvis HUD (\"doesn't look like my site\") — his site's character is editorial lowercase, mono accents, monochrome restraint. Final approach (fb9a470): typography/voice port, not just colors — lowercase black wordmark + caret, mono green panel titles (site h3 style), no panel header bars, monochrome tag chips replaced rainbow inline-styled chips (edited app.js newsItemHtml), stat labels mono lowercase, pills mono lowercase, orb removed from loading. Lesson: when Hugo says \"make it look like my site\" he means the TYPOGRAPHY and restraint, not the palette swap." issue=#21 tags=epic3,design,user-feedback,lesson
